ome  time so you know we don't want to freak  people out we don't want to scare people  we don't want to contribute to the  greater anxiety but we want people to be  informed that this is a big deal Gail  it's important to remember as we monitor  patients going forward for concerns with  other organ systems  we can't forget about the psychological  system we know that in patients who  survived critical care illnesses or been  in the ICU they are at risk for  development of PTSD or depression so  important for families providers friends  to really be aware of that as well as  the patient's themselves as a doctor  Tara I can't imagine what it's like for  doctors to see one of their own recover  because you all know exactly how hard  that might have been for that particular  person that was great video thank you  dr. Tara Narula
 

